<stringmatch name="calleepop-x86-16 #1: with the constant 4 the local becomes a third argument of the near call" min="1" max="1">^  v1 = addtwo\(7,5,9\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleepop-x86-16 #2: with the constant 4 the final add reads the call's result instead of the local" min="1" max="1">^  return farf\(\) \+ v1;$</stringmatch>
